SOLAR ROOFTOP INSTALLATION GUIDE
Solar panels convert sunlight into electricity through photovoltaic cells. Before installation, a technician should inspect the roof condition, orientation, shading, and available area. Panels are mounted on secure supports and connected to an inverter that converts direct current into usable alternating current. Regular cleaning and electrical inspections help maintain performance.

A household can monitor energy production through a meter or a digital monitoring application. The system may reduce electricity bills and lower dependence on power generated from fossil fuels.